194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (1. Feature Engineering: We calculate the Rate of Change of Frequency \(RoCoF\) via numerical differentiation \(dF/dt\) across the time steps to capture the physical velocity of grid transients. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (2. Cleaning: We apply Z-score normalization to all continuous features to ensure equal mathematical weighting and stability during the Ridge matrix inversion. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (3. Transformation: We discard the binary Class_Label to formally shift the dataset architecture from discrete classification to continuous time-series regression. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (4. Windowing: We apply a sliding-window technique k=10 to combine the telemetry from t-9 through t into a single, flattened feature vector used to predict the target frequency at t+1.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
